<p class="no-indent" style="text-align:center; color:#888; font-size:15px; margin-bottom:30px;">Based on LM I:24 (continued)<br/>Tachlis HaYdi'ah ֲ· Nine Haichalos ֲ· Sh'kalim ֲ· Zachor ֲ· Parah</p>

<h3>ֲ§15</h3>

<p>The principle: the essential tikkun of all worlds is through <span class="bold-concept">placing action before hearing</span> (= emunah) ג€” performing all mitzvos with great simchah through emunah alone, even without understanding any reason. Through this ג€” through simchas hamitzvah ג€” one ascends higher and higher until drawing <span class="transliteration">bircas hasaichel</span> <span class="bracket-def">[the blessing of intellect]</span> and rectifying the M'sader v'haM'yashev (= Keser) ג†’ through the pursuit and restraint ג†’ attaining the nine Haichalos ג†’ perceiving His Elokus (= the Ain Sof) in matai v'lo matai = <span class="key-term">tachlis haydi'ah asher lo naida</span>.</p>

<p>No true hasagah of His Elokus is possible except through receiving the M'sader v'haM'yashev from Keser (the restraint of the Mochin) ג†’ the Ain Sof in matai v'lo matai ג†’ the nine Haichalos. This M'sader can only be attained through <span class="transliteration">asiyah</span> and <span class="transliteration">uvda</span> <span class="bracket-def">[practical deed]</span> specifically ג€” mitzvos with simchah. Then precisely ג€” through pursuit and restraint ג€” one attains the Ain Sof = tachlis haydi'ah asher lo naida.</p>

<p>This ultimate level ג€” only the very greatest Tzaddikim attain it. Though everyone says "tachlis haydi'ah asher lo naida," no one truly knows the meaning of this in completeness except one who grasps it ג€” who merits it through his good deeds. <span class="bold-concept">As I understood from the mouth of Rabbainu z"l</span>, as explained in his holy Sichos. When one merits this: the ydi'ah and the absence of ydi'ah are all one ג€” through both together the ydi'ah and hasagah are completed. The "<span class="transliteration">lo naida</span>" itself (the absence of ydi'ah) is itself the ydi'ah. In truth, no one understands this in completeness except those who merit it ג€” fortunate are they! The ydi'ah and its absence = the pursuit and the restraint (truly one) ג†’ through both ג†’ hasagah in matai v'lo matai ג†’ the nine Haichalos ("<span class="transliteration">d'lais man dikiyama v'hu v'lo mis'dabkin v'lo ydi'in</span>" ג€” "none stands in them, they do not cling, they are not known").</p>

<p>Whoever merits this hasagah ג€” he <span class="key-term">rectifies the sin of Adam HaRishon</span> and nullifies sitra d'mosa (= the Sitra Achra = denials = "bikshu cheshbonos rabim" drawn from the p'gam of the Aitz HaDa'as). As Rashi explains on: "<span class="transliteration">Asah ha'Elokim es ha'adam yashar v'haimah bikshu cheshbonos rabim</span>" ג€” "God made man straight, but they sought many calculations" <span class="source">(Koheles 7)</span> ג€” referring to the sin of Adam HaRishon. The Zohar says: he gazed where he had no permission. He had not yet rectified the M'sader v'haM'yashev ג†’ he was forbidden to leaven his mind in his hasagah, forbidden to pursue and investigate what he had no right to ג†’ he should have believed in Hashem and kept His commandment not to eat from the Aitz HaDa'as. He transgressed ג€” doubted Hashem and His mitzvos ג€” ate from the Aitz HaDa'as and gazed where he had no permission ג†’ death was decreed for all generations. He wanted to know the root of good and evil before rectifying the M'sader ג†’ he fell into denials. He was the aspect of "<span class="transliteration">nirgan mafrid Aluf</span>" ג€” he separated the <span class="transliteration">Aluf</span> of the world (= Keser = <span class="transliteration">Peleh</span> = <span class="transliteration">Alef</span>) ג€” he separated the pursuit from the restraint ג†’ Da'as shattered and nullified completely. No one can attain complete hasagah of matai v'lo matai ג€” only the very few greatest Tzaddikim who purified themselves entirely from <span class="transliteration">zuhamas haNachash</span>, rectifying Adam's sin through performing mitzvos with simchah in emunah alone ג†’ attaining the Keser ג†’ the nine Haichalos ג†’ the Ain Sof.</p>

<h3>ֲ§16</h3>

<p>"<span class="transliteration">Ki sisa es rosh B'nay Yisrael lifkudaihem... v'lo yihyeh vahem negef bifkod osam</span>" <span class="source">(Shemos 30)</span>. When counting Yisrael, protection is needed so that <span class="transliteration">sitra d'mosa</span> does not take hold through the <span class="transliteration">minyan</span> <span class="bracket-def">[counting]</span>. The Sitra Achra (= sitra d'mosa) holds on through minyan ג€” "bikshu cheshbonos rabim." Hashem is beyond number and counting: "<span class="transliteration">Lifnay echad mah atah sofair</span>" ג€” "Before the One, what do you count?" All <span class="key-term">number and counting (= multiplicity)</span> begins only after the Creation ג€” since after Creation there are many aspects and details, and there counting applies.</p>

<p>How multiplicity (number/counting) emerges from the Source of Unity ג€” how diverse phenomena flow from the utterly Simple One ג€” this cannot be grasped by any human intellect. It can only be held through <span class="transliteration">emunah</span> drawn to us by the great Tzaddikim who merit the nine Haichalos. These Tzaddikim <span class="bold-concept">include and unify</span> all of Creation (= number/counting = after Creation) back into before-Creation ג€” the root of Unity. They perceive His Elokus and Unity in matai v'lo matai, through pursuit and restraint ג†’ the nine Haichalos are formed.</p>

<p>These nine Haichalos in their supernal root are exceedingly lofty and hidden ג€” they are the <span class="transliteration">Oros haTzachtzachos</span> <span class="bracket-def">[Lights of the Brilliances]</span>, above the S'firos. Yet through the pursuit striking against the restraint, they become, as it were, <span class="key-term">Haichalos within the hasagah in the aspect of number and counting</span> ג€” for they are <span class="bold-concept">nine</span> Haichalos. These nine Haichalos (= root of the S'firos) are the root of all number and counting in the world. They are specifically <span class="key-term">nine</span> ג€” because nine is the root of all number. Visibly: counting ends at nine; after nine it returns to the source of Unity (ten = one unit of ten; then counting continues to ninety, returns again to one hundred = one; and so on forever). The root of number = nine; afterward everything returns and is included in Unity.</p>

<p>This is the truth: number and counting always return and are included in His Unity ג€” the essential tikkun of all worlds. The root of number derives from His Unity through the nine Haichalos (formed through pursuit and restraint = matai v'lo matai = <span class="transliteration">ratzo vashov, ratzo vashov</span>) ג€” always returning and being included in His Unity, never separating from the Source. Therefore they are only nine Haichalos: after reaching nine, they return in ratzo vashov (matai v'lo matai) ג†’ included in His Unity. These nine Haichalos (root of all number) are bound and unified in His Unity. Whoever merits this hasagah ג†’ all denials nullified, sitra d'mosa nullified ("bikshu cheshbonos rabim" from multiplicity) ג€” for this Tzaddik includes all number and counting back into the source of Unity through the nine Haichalos.</p>

<p>This is the mitzvah of <span class="key-term">Sh'kalim</span> for korbanos tzibbur and Ketores. Through Sh'kalim ג†’ korbanos and Ketores ג†’ simchah is drawn ("<span class="transliteration">Ketores y'samach laiv</span>"; korbanos associated with simchah in many p'sukim) ג†’ kedushah raised from k'lipos ג†’ nine Haichalos attained ג†’ sitra d'mosa (holding onto number) nullified ג†’ number included in His Unity.</p>

<p>Therefore the Torah commanded giving Sh'kalim during the counting ג€” so there would be no negef. The sitra d'mosa seizing the minyan is nullified through the Sh'kalim (= korbanos/Ketores = simchas hamitzvah) ג†’ minyan included in His Unity through the nine Haichalos.</p>

<h3>ֲ§17</h3>

<p>"<span class="transliteration">Machatzis hashekel</span>" ג€” "<span class="key-term">half</span> the shekel" specifically. "<span class="transliteration">Machatzis hashekel t'rumah laHashem</span>" ג€” "a half-shekel, a gift to Hashem." The wondrous hasagah of the nine Haichalos (merited through Sh'kalim = simchas hamitzvah) is in the aspect of <span class="bold-concept">machatzis hashekel</span> = matai v'lo matai = pursuit and restraint. One must always <span class="key-term">stand upon the scale</span>: if he pursues to attain more than befitting his level ג€” the hasagah is completely nullified (too much oil extinguishes the lamp). If he completely restrains and prevents the hasagah ג€” he attains nothing at all. Therefore this hasagah is in the aspect of machatzis hashekel ג€” one must always tip the scale upward, to be included in His Unity in ratzo vashov = <span class="transliteration">machatzis hashekel t'rumah laHashem</span>. Fortunate is the one who merits this!</p>

<p>Therefore they were commanded to give Sh'kalim at the erection of the <span class="transliteration">Mishkan</span>. All the chambers and vessels of the Mishkan and Bais HaMikdash = vessels and Haichalos of kedushah deriving from the supernal Haichalos ג€” whose root is the nine Haichalos (through which one attains His Elokus, merited through simchas hamitzvah = Sh'kalim). Hence Sh'kalim were commanded for building the Mishkan ג€” the Mishkan (= Haichalos) is built through simchas hamitzvah (= Sh'kalim). The Torah in LM I:24 explains on "<span class="transliteration">Mikdash Hashem kon'nu yadecha</span>" ג€” "The Sanctuary, Hashem, Your hands established" ג€” that the Mikdash = bircas hasaichel. The essential hasagah of Elokus was in the Bais HaMikdash and Mishkan: "<span class="transliteration">V'no'adti l'cha sham</span>" ג€” "I will meet with you there" <span class="source">(Shemos 25)</span>.</p>

<h3>ֲ§18</h3>

<p>Therefore after <span class="key-term">Parshas Sh'kalim</span> we read <span class="key-term">Parshas Zachor</span> ג€” the aspect of wiping out Amalak and Haman <span class="transliteration">yimach sh'mo</span> <span class="bracket-def">[may his name be erased]</span>. They = the denials of the investigators = the essential <span class="transliteration">zuhamas haNachash</span> = sitra d'mosa. Haman's intense hold in these denials (= sitra d'mosa) is why he wished, chas v'shalom, to intensify and kill and destroy all Yisrael. Hashem Himself annulled his counsel and corrupted his plan and wiped him from the world ג€” <span class="bold-concept">through the power of the Sh'kalim of Yisrael</span> (= simchas hamitzvah ג†’ all k'lipos nullified). As the Sages said <span class="source">(Megillah 13)</span>: "<span class="transliteration">Rasha! K'var kadmu shiklaihem l'sh'kalecha</span>" ג€” "Wicked one! Their Sh'kalim already preceded yours!"</p>

<h3>ֲ§19</h3>

<p>Afterward we read <span class="key-term">Parshas Parah</span>, which purifies from <span class="transliteration">tumas mais</span> <span class="bracket-def">[the impurity of death]</span>. Parshas Parah Adumah reveals to us that it is impossible to understand any reason for the mitzvos of the Creator, and it is forbidden to contemplate this at all. "<span class="transliteration">Zos chukas haTorah</span>" ג€” "This is the statute of the Torah" <span class="source">(Bamidbar 19)</span>. As Rashi explains: since the Satan and the nations taunt Yisrael ג€” "What is this mitzvah? What reason does it have?" ג€” therefore it is written "<span class="transliteration">chukah</span>" ג€” "A statute I have decreed, a decree I have decreed ג€” <span class="bold-concept">you have no permission to question it</span>."</p>

<p>This mitzvah was not stated to teach about itself alone but about the entirety ג€” to reveal and instruct regarding all the mitzvos of the Torah: it is forbidden to investigate reasons at all. Therefore all the other mitzvos are also called <span class="transliteration">chukim</span>: "<span class="transliteration">V'hachukim v'hasToros</span>" ג€” Rashi: "such as eating pig and wearing sha'atnez ג€” the nations taunt Yisrael that these have no reason." In truth, the reasons for the mitzvos are hidden and concealed ג€” impossible to grasp through any human intellect. One must fulfill them through emunah alone ג€” believing in Hashem and in Moshe His servant, as all Yisrael believe, with <span class="transliteration">p'shitus</span>, without the ways of their foolish "wisdom" ג€” those who wish to investigate and understand how Hashem spoke with Moshe (which is forbidden even to put in writing, much less to speak ג€” their alien, rotten, filthy opinions are more full of filth than a latrine, and no stench in the world is worse).</p>

<p><span class="key-term">Parah Adumah purifies from tumas mais</span> because it is the aspect of "<span class="transliteration">Amarti echk'mah v'hi r'chokah mimeni</span>" ג€” "I said I would become wise, but it is far from me" <span class="source">(Koheles 7)</span>. It purifies the impure and makes the pure impure ג€” which certainly cannot be understood by any human intellect. Yet it purifies from tumas mais ג€” the essential tumah being the <span class="transliteration">chakiras</span> of the investigators and deniers (= sitra d'mosa = zuhamas haNachash). Through the mitzvah of Parah (= <span class="transliteration">chukas haTorah</span> ג€” revealing that the Torah is a <span class="transliteration">chukah</span>, "I said I would become wise but it is far," "you have no permission to question") ג†’ one is purified from tumas mais ג†’ sitra d'mosa nullified ג€” through believing in Hashem and His mitzvos without investigating any reason, fulfilling them as a <span class="transliteration">chukah</span> alone (= the essence of emunah) ג†’ meriting simchah ג†’ attaining the nine Haichalos in matai v'lo matai.</p>

<p>There, pursuit and restraint are included together in great unity ג€” all opposites are included and unified ג†’ all included in His Unity. There is the root of the secret of Parah Adumah: <span class="key-term">two opposites in one subject</span> ג€” purifying the impure and making the pure impure. This derives from the secret of pursuit and restraint. Since Adam HaRishon damaged this and separated the pursuit from the restraint through eating from the Aitz HaDa'as ג†’ death and tumah were drawn into the world ג†’ all opposites that cannot be grasped (all <span class="transliteration">kushyos</span> are from opposites: the question of <span class="transliteration">ydi'ah</span> <span class="bracket-def">[foreknowledge]</span> and <span class="transliteration">b'chirah</span> <span class="bracket-def">[free will]</span> and the like ג€” appearing as two opposites in one subject). But we believe all is truly correct and right ג€” not truly opposites at all; only due to Adam's sin, our physicality, and our own sins can we not understand how these opposites are included together.</p>

<p>Through the mitzvah of Parah specifically ג€” fulfilling His mitzvos despite containing two opposites (purifying impure, making pure impure ג€” certainly impossible to understand), keeping it through emunah alone ג†’ we draw emunah upon ourselves to fulfill all His mitzvos and statutes without any reason at all ג†’ purified from tumas mais (= chakiros and denials). Through fulfilling mitzvos in emunah alone (= the essence of simchah) ג†’ included in the nine Haichalos ג†’ all opposites included together. In the future this hasagah will be revealed ג€” our enemies will see and be ashamed ג€” and we will rejoice and exult in Hashem: "<span class="transliteration">V'atah tagil baHashem bikdosh Yisrael tis'halal</span>" ג€” "You will rejoice in Hashem, in the Holy One of Yisrael you will glory" <span class="source">(Y'shayah 41)</span>.</p>

